# Build outputs
build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
*.asi
!examples/**/*.asi  # keep examples if any
*.dll
!vendor/**/*.dll
!examples/**/*.dll  # example plugin DLLs ship via release zips
*.exe
*.pdb
*.exp
*.lib
*.obj
*.o
*.a
# Compiled Java from the vendored BLAKE3 self-test (javac output; regenerated
# from the tracked .java sources by the run recipe in Blake3SelfTest.java).
*.class

# Python bytecode caches (auto-generated when scripts run; never useful in git).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE / tooling
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# Logs
*.log

# Local artifacts not for source control
# _download/ — cached downloads (ULAH zip etc.); regenerated by build/release scripts
# release-staging/ — generated drag-drop release; produced by release scripts
# test-install/ — local staging area used when iterating against the live game
_download/
release-staging/
test-install/

# Transient per-session runtime lock (sessionId/pid/timestamp) — never committed.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# This file is the PRIVATE repo's ignore list — ordinary git semantics. The
# private working materials (.claude/, CLAUDE.md, _research/, third-party-ghidra/
# scripts, test-fixtures/, docs/) are TRACKED here, not ignored. The private/public
# split is NOT enforced by this file: publish-public.ps1 uses an ALLOWLIST (it
# publishes only its listed public dirs + root files; everything else, including
# this .gitignore, stays private by default).
#
# What stays ignored below is only genuinely heavy / reproducible binaries inside
# the otherwise-tracked private trees, so the private repo holds the scripts and
# notes without carrying gigabytes of third-party toolchain.

# third-party-ghidra/: track the scripts + README; ignore the toolchain binaries
# and the multi-GB analyzed project DB (clone-and-go expects these present locally).
third-party-ghidra/ghidra_project/
third-party-ghidra/ghidra_12.1_PUBLIC/
third-party-ghidra/x64dbg/
third-party-ghidra/ninja/
third-party-ghidra/WHGame.dll
third-party-ghidra/*.fidb

# test-fixtures/: track the probe sources + manifests; ignore built .pak blobs.
test-fixtures/pak-mods/**/*.pak

# _research/: tracked (recon notes, scripts, wiki cache). Predecessor-sig clones
# are shallow clones of third-party repos — keep them on disk, out of git.
_research/predecessor-sigs/

# refdata-extractor sandbox: the matcher CODE + the make_sandbox recipe are
# tracked; the fixture DATA (a real WHGame.dll dump slice + the authored v2
# mutation + backups) is derived/local and never committed (it would also leak
# game-binary-derived content to the public allowlist). Regenerable via
# make_sandbox.py.
data/refdata-extractor/sandbox/v1/
data/refdata-extractor/sandbox/v2/
data/refdata-extractor/sandbox/v1.backup/
data/refdata-extractor/sandbox/v2.backup/
data/refdata-extractor/sandbox/ground_truth.csv

# refdata-extractor dump dirs: each refdata-<game-version>/ is ~1.3 GB of
# Ghidra-extracted CSVs per game version, derived from a copy of WHGame.dll
# and regenerable via run-parallel.ps1. The dump/README.md placeholder is
# tracked (documents the dir's purpose + naming convention); the
# refdata-<version>/ subdirs are not.
data/refdata-extractor/dump/refdata-*/

# data/reference.sqlite + data/reference-dev.sqlite -- generated SQLite DBs
# produced by data/refdata-extractor/python/import_to_sqlite.py from a local
# dump under data/refdata-extractor/dump/refdata-<game-version>/. The schema
# docs at data/reference.md + data/reference-dev.md are tracked (public);
# the .sqlite blobs are derived artifacts that ship via the release page
# (USER + DEV), never committed.
data/reference.sqlite
data/reference-dev.sqlite

# data/maintainer-tool/.maintainer-tool-cache.json -- the seed editor's
# per-machine link table (per-module DLL paths on the maintainer's local disk
# + recent-paths history). Per-machine state, never committed. See
# data/maintainer-tool/requirements.md R12.
data/maintainer-tool/.maintainer-tool-cache.json

# data/maintainer-tool/ -- the maintainer tool (FastAPI backend + React
# frontend + Dockerfile + operator docs) is its OWN git repository, nested at
# this path but NOT part of the kcdx tree: it pushes to its own remote
# (kcdx-maintainer-tool), carries its own ignore list + license, and keeps its
# source/history out of kcdx's history, build gate, and publish allowlist.
# kcdx never tracks it. (The frontend is a further nested repo inside it.)
data/maintainer-tool/

# test-plugins/probe-asset-overlay/ -- THROWAWAY step-3a asset-overlay redirect
# probe. Contains game-asset-derived bytes (the _extracted/ real game files +
# the .lua/.dds substitutes derived from them), so it must NEVER be committed
# (copyrighted game assets + test-plugins/ is public-allowlisted). Its signal is
# the dev log, not a committed artifact; the dir is removed with the probe
# instrumentation at step 3b.
test-plugins/probe-asset-overlay/